@startuml
title ParametricCAD — Undo / Redo architecture

skinparam shadowing false

actor User
participant MainWindow
participant QUndoStack as Stack
participant "QUndoCommand" as Command
participant Body
participant "ParametricFeature history" as History
participant ModelPresenter as Presenter
participant CadViewer as Viewer
participant FeatureEditorPanel as Panel

User -> MainWindow : Ctrl+Z / Ctrl+Y
MainWindow -> Stack : undo() / redo()
Stack -> Command : undo() / redo()
Command -> Body : add/remove feature or change parameter
Body -> History : mark dirty and recompute
History --> Body : restored/generated shapes
Stack -> MainWindow : indexChanged()
MainWindow -> Presenter : refreshModelView()
Presenter -> Body : recompute()
Presenter -> Viewer : update presentations
Presenter -> Viewer : apply visibility policy
MainWindow -> Panel : refresh descriptors
MainWindow -> Panel : preserve valid selection IDs

note right of Command
  Commands retain stable feature identity
  and old/new model state.

  Push/Pull is represented by
  PushPullFeature and uses the existing
  AddFeatureCommand path.
end note

note over Viewer,Panel
  Undo/Redo is model-driven.
  UI observes the common refresh path;
  it has no private Push/Pull history.
end note
@enduml
